@ "decimal" {
  "##": Decimal

  "body" = ```markdown
Notation as value: `1.1`, `1.10`, `1e3`

Fractional literals without a suffix are exact decimals. The written scale is kept (`1.10`
stays `1.10`), while equality is numeric (`1.10` equals `1.1`). A float schema reads a decimal as
the nearest float; add an `f32`/`f64` suffix to write a float directly.
```

}

@ "bytes" {
  "##": Bytes

  "body" = ```markdown
Notation as value: `` base64`SGVsbG8=` `` or `` hex`48656c6c6f` ``

The `base64` and `hex` language tags are reserved for binary data, in inline code and in code
blocks. Whitespace inside the encoded data is ignored, so long values can be wrapped in a code
block. The encoding is only notation: the two examples above are the same value.
```

}

@ "set" {
  "##": Set

  "body" = ```markdown
Notation as value: `#{"a", 1, (2, "b")}`, `#{}`

An unordered collection of unique values. Elements are integers, strings, or tuples of those
(the same values allowed as map keys). Order is ignored when comparing sets, and duplicate
elements are an error.
```

}

